It does not live up to the standards that people have become accustomed to in this place.

2709
02:55:07,470 --> 02:55:08,210
There we go.

2710
02:55:08,370 --> 02:55:08,970
Clean that up.

2711
02:55:15,270 --> 02:55:16,010
Oh-ho!

2712
02:55:21,300 --> 02:55:21,780
Come here.

2713
02:55:23,700 --> 02:55:25,500
Also, I just realized I forgot my shield.

2714
02:55:26,760 --> 02:55:29,700
I'm kind of glad I went into combat with that dude just now, so I realized.

2715
02:55:45,160 --> 02:55:46,080
Where did I put that?

2716
02:55:51,380 --> 02:55:51,800
Nice.

2717
02:55:51,800 --> 02:55:52,460
Hammer ready.

2718
02:55:58,380 --> 02:55:58,800
Shit.

2719
02:56:01,060 --> 02:56:02,380
Okay, this thing is weird.

2720
02:56:04,660 --> 02:56:06,780
I gotta go back to that biome as well.

2721
02:56:06,980 --> 02:56:11,040
Experiment some more, because I was there only briefly, and it's kinda creepy, and it's weird.

2722
02:56:14,390 --> 02:56:16,150
It warrants further exploration.

2723
02:56:18,650 --> 02:56:19,830
All my boats are gone.

2724
02:56:23,870 --> 02:56:24,550
Here we go.

2725
02:56:28,650 --> 02:56:29,450
Oh, no, wait.

2726
02:56:30,930 --> 02:56:32,590
Uh... Oh, do I need shears for this?

2727
02:56:33,870 --> 02:56:35,530
Oh, I don't want to go back again.

2728
02:56:36,390 --> 02:56:37,470
I may have to go back again.

2729
02:56:39,070 --> 02:56:39,390
Goddammit.

2730
02:56:39,470 --> 02:56:39,730
You know what?

2731
02:56:39,730 --> 02:56:41,250
I'm also going to bring my hoe, just in case.

2732
02:56:44,640 --> 02:56:50,380
Because if I actually do end up finding vines, I don't want to be in the situation where I can't bring them with me.

2733
02:56:52,620 --> 02:56:55,800
Let's just bring all the apparatuses that we know about with us.

2734
02:56:57,260 --> 02:56:58,200
Just to be safe.

2735
02:57:06,120 --> 02:57:06,540
Utility.

2736
02:57:08,260 --> 02:57:09,240
Shovel we have.

2737
02:57:12,060 --> 02:57:13,440
I'll bring a brush as well.

2738
02:57:14,920 --> 02:57:15,800
You never know.

2739
02:57:18,400 --> 02:57:19,440
A golden hole.

2740
02:57:19,680 --> 02:57:20,700
No, give me this one.

2741
02:57:22,540 --> 02:57:25,980
And... also bring... Where is the shear?

2742
02:57:32,750 --> 02:57:34,270
I have no clue where I left that.

2743
02:57:34,650 --> 02:57:35,350
Make a new one.

2744
02:57:36,650 --> 02:57:37,570
I remember how.

2745
02:57:38,570 --> 02:57:39,010
Yeah.

2746
02:57:41,430 --> 02:57:41,870
Sweetcakes.

2747
02:57:47,010 --> 02:57:47,450
Grass.

2748
02:57:49,090 --> 02:57:50,670
Spruce can stay at home.

2749
02:57:51,610 --> 02:57:52,710
In this chest over here.

2750
02:57:53,990 --> 02:57:55,230
And we have enough food as well.

2751
02:57:55,430 --> 02:57:56,130
So many steaks.

2752
02:58:04,310 --> 02:58:04,710
Ho.

2753
02:58:04,710 --> 02:58:05,110
Shears.

2754
02:58:05,490 --> 02:58:09,090
Is there anything else I could potentially... need?

2755
02:58:10,950 --> 02:58:12,850
Maybe a... honestly, maybe a bucket.

2756
02:58:15,010 --> 02:58:17,230
I don't know how or why, but maybe it's a thing.

2757
02:58:17,410 --> 02:58:19,630
You know, where you can pick up something on the water with the bucket.

2758
02:58:20,150 --> 02:58:22,590
Some kind of viney thing on the water.

2759
02:58:24,950 --> 02:58:25,790
Oh, I have a bucket.

2760
02:58:25,950 --> 02:58:26,850
I have a bucket already.

2761
02:58:27,890 --> 02:58:28,810
Alright, everything's fine.

2762
02:58:28,990 --> 02:58:29,450
We're off.

2763
02:58:34,970 --> 02:58:35,990
Nice.

2764
02:58:43,350 --> 02:58:44,430
I really like these.

2765
02:58:45,530 --> 02:58:46,850
That is the best thing ever.

2766
02:58:49,210 --> 02:58:52,050
I feel like my village is really starting to come together.

2767
02:58:52,690 --> 02:58:56,630
It is kind of embarrassing that I still haven't furnished my own house yet.

2768
02:58:57,970 --> 02:58:59,950
But you know, I think that shows character.

2769
02:59:00,730 --> 02:59:06,370
I chose to furnish the houses of my followers in the village before I furnish my own.

2770
02:59:06,970 --> 02:59:07,450
Right?

2771
02:59:09,110 --> 02:59:10,410
They know my priorities.

2772
02:59:10,880 --> 02:59:12,660
I care about my subjects.

2773
02:59:14,080 --> 02:59:19,100
And their well-being, and... I don't want them to feel like they need to escape, you know?

2774
02:59:19,220 --> 02:59:20,040
This is not a prison.

2775
02:59:21,160 --> 02:59:24,420
They can stay or they can leave, but I would rather they stay.

2776
02:59:24,780 --> 02:59:25,940
Of their own volition.

2777
02:59:27,180 --> 02:59:28,140
Okay, let's see here.

2778
02:59:29,900 --> 02:59:30,380
Ho.

2779
02:59:33,730 --> 02:59:34,630
Doesn't work.

2780
02:59:35,110 --> 02:59:35,750
Shears?

2781
02:59:37,390 --> 02:59:38,030
What?

2782
02:59:39,090 --> 02:59:40,370
No fucking way.

2783
02:59:41,410 --> 02:59:42,430
Ah, wait, wait!

2784
02:59:43,370 --> 02:59:44,010
Seagrass.

2785
02:59:47,230 --> 02:59:47,870
Right.

2786
02:59:48,830 --> 02:59:53,130
Makes sense that I can only put it on... the ocean floor.

2787
02:59:57,100 --> 02:59:58,600
Only some of them give me... Look!

2788
03:00:00,820 --> 03:00:01,600
Isn't that weird?

2789
03:00:03,420 --> 03:00:03,820
Huh.

2790
03:00:05,960 --> 03:00:07,720
I don't think this can be put on walls, though.

2791
03:00:09,360 --> 03:00:10,440
No, it cannot.

2792
03:00:13,640 --> 03:00:16,760
I... I gotta find... Man, where have I seen this?

2793
03:00:16,780 --> 03:00:17,580
I've seen it before.

2794
03:00:18,480 --> 03:00:20,180
I've seen things growing on the side.

2795
03:00:20,360 --> 03:00:22,420
Maybe I'm actually... I'm just thinking of moss.

2796
03:00:32,200 --> 03:00:33,380
What else do I need right now?

2797
03:00:35,040 --> 03:00:35,440
Experience.

2798
03:00:37,920 --> 03:00:39,240
Oh, I want to go remove that.

2799
03:00:40,560 --> 03:00:42,040
Don't have enough ascension blocks with me.

2800
03:00:42,080 --> 03:00:42,980
I should have brought some dirt.

2801
03:00:44,360 --> 03:00:47,380
Just to remove this disgusting creation.

2802
03:00:50,550 --> 03:00:52,770
Although I am thinking of making some kind of tower out here.

2803
03:00:53,510 --> 03:00:54,630
You know, in the middle of the ocean?

2804
03:00:54,750 --> 03:00:55,530
Just something cool.

2805
03:00:56,770 --> 03:01:00,570
Like a watchtower or maybe a... what do you call those things with a light on them?

2806
03:01:00,850 --> 03:01:01,510
A lighthouse?

2807
03:01:03,350 --> 03:01:07,730
I also have an idea of how I may make a lighthouse that has a rotating beacon on top.

2808
03:01:10,430 --> 03:01:11,230
With redstone.

2809
03:01:13,150 --> 03:01:14,510
Maybe that's the next thing I want to do.

2810
03:01:16,430 --> 03:01:17,070
Not here, though.

2811
03:01:17,130 --> 03:01:18,010
That would have to be on land.

2812
03:01:18,170 --> 03:01:18,790
So maybe...

2813
03:01:20,100 --> 03:01:22,360
Maybe like over there at the tip of that.

2814
03:01:30,280 --> 03:01:32,700
Kinda wanna bring home some of that stone that I see over there.

2815
03:01:32,980 --> 03:01:33,340
Yeah.

2816
03:01:34,180 --> 03:01:35,420
This is part of that mission.

2817
03:01:35,700 --> 03:01:39,680
We're gonna find mossy cobblestone, mossy, uh, whatever the fuck.

2818
03:01:40,020 --> 03:01:40,560
Just mossy.

2819
03:01:41,100 --> 03:01:41,960
Everything mossy.

2820
03:01:43,040 --> 03:01:45,460
And also modify that bridge, of course.

2821
03:01:46,140 --> 03:01:47,520
Make it look a bit better.

2822
03:01:49,740 --> 03:01:52,120
We need lights on it, and we gotta continue the railway.

2823
03:01:57,240 --> 03:01:58,260
That looks so good.

2824
03:02:01,780 --> 03:02:04,600
One of my favorite creations is that bridge.

2825
03:02:05,360 --> 03:02:06,380
I'm so proud of it.

2826
03:02:13,100 --> 03:02:15,020
Oh yeah, there's weird sounds here now.

2827
03:02:21,940 --> 03:02:22,680
And that.

2828
03:02:35,720 --> 03:02:40,060
The reason I'm destroying this down here and not up here, I don't want to destroy the natural landscape too much.

2829
03:02:40,240 --> 03:02:43,880
If anything, I should go further away from home before I do this.

2830
03:02:46,020 --> 03:02:47,500
I kind of like the way this looks.

2831
03:02:47,800 --> 03:02:49,460
You know, close to home, it looks nice.

2832
03:02:51,260 --> 03:02:52,340
Don't shit where you eat.

2833
03:02:58,540 --> 03:03:00,080
Probably somewhere downstairs, I don't care.

2834
03:03:06,860 --> 03:03:09,080
Oh yeah, we had the underwater thing over here too.

2835
03:03:09,820 --> 03:03:10,600
Never did finish that.

2836
03:03:10,760 --> 03:03:11,380
Let's try going down.

2837
03:03:15,520 --> 03:03:16,260
Look at that.

2838
03:03:17,180 --> 03:03:18,500
Hey, that's pretty sick actually.

2839
03:03:19,880 --> 03:03:23,600
One day we're gonna ride this railway and it will be glorious.

2840
03:03:25,120 --> 03:03:26,460
Let's just make some headroom here.

2841
03:03:44,190 --> 03:03:45,130
I need my boat.

2842
03:03:48,070 --> 03:03:48,550
Dude!

2843
03:03:49,710 --> 03:03:52,750
Is that a way to prevent fall damage if you're fast enough?

2844
03:03:53,510 --> 03:03:56,590
Putting down the boat and getting in the boat while mid-fall.

2845
03:03:57,730 --> 03:03:59,330
That could actually be the thing.

2846
03:04:04,880 --> 03:04:07,160
See, I'm starting to see stuff like this over there.

2847
03:04:07,760 --> 03:04:08,940
That could look good at home.

2848
03:04:09,560 --> 03:04:09,960
Garnish.

2849
03:04:11,500 --> 03:04:12,780
Or maybe just some grass.

2850
03:04:12,960 --> 03:04:13,920
Dude, just some grass!

2851
03:04:15,740 --> 03:04:16,960
Good old grass!

2852
03:04:18,200 --> 03:04:18,600
Hello?

2853
03:04:18,900 --> 03:04:20,940
This is like the thing on the water, but it's on land.

2854
03:04:24,860 --> 03:04:27,360
Uh... Yes!

2855
03:04:29,800 --> 03:04:30,200
Yes!

2856
03:04:34,160 --> 03:04:35,540
Oh my god.

2857
03:04:39,400 --> 03:04:41,640
This stuff is... grass.

2858
03:04:42,740 --> 03:04:44,820
I'm about to bust my ass.

2859
03:04:48,420 --> 03:04:49,580
Oh, I need to go to bed.

2860
03:05:03,450 --> 03:05:04,550
Bro, I can't... there.

2861
03:05:06,330 --> 03:05:06,970
Found it.

2862
03:05:08,050 --> 03:05:09,850
Oh yeah, it's much easier to see it now, too.

2863
03:05:11,690 --> 03:05:15,350
I don't know, after sleeping, man, it's like the grass stands out way more.

2864
03:05:16,510 --> 03:05:17,710
You can't explain that.

2865
03:05:19,150 --> 03:05:22,250
Getting a good night's rest really helps with the vision.

2866
03:05:24,110 --> 03:05:25,870
It's like your eyes grow tired or something.

2867
03:05:27,150 --> 03:05:27,630
Hello?

2868
03:05:28,150 --> 03:05:28,630
Skeleton?

2869
03:05:33,220 --> 03:05:33,700
Dankeschön.

2870
03:05:35,600 --> 03:05:36,800
Oh, and... Yes!

2871
03:05:36,960 --> 03:05:37,260
Oh, dude!

2872
03:05:37,480 --> 03:05:38,980
We're just gonna plant random flowers, too!

2873
03:05:40,660 --> 03:05:42,100
Random-ass flowers everywhere.

2874
03:05:48,900 --> 03:05:51,580
This reminds me of playing, uh, the craft mine now.

2875
03:05:52,420 --> 03:05:53,220
Remember that?

2876
03:05:57,140 --> 03:05:58,580
This is what I did, basically.

2877
03:06:07,960 --> 03:06:09,960
It's called short grass, this is called seagrass.

2878
03:06:11,100 --> 03:06:12,720
Makes a lot of sense, doesn't it?

2879
03:06:13,940 --> 03:06:15,320
I did not bring my boat with me.

2880
03:06:16,800 --> 03:06:17,620
Can I shear you?

2881
03:06:22,000 --> 03:06:23,680
I would love to shear your feathers.

2882
03:06:30,140 --> 03:06:33,540
Like, I just want to, you know, get the feathers and not anything else.

2883
03:06:35,860 --> 03:06:37,620
Maybe that actually hurts them.

2884
03:06:37,720 --> 03:06:38,040
I don't know.

2885
03:06:42,140 --> 03:06:42,520
Hey!

2886
03:06:55,520 --> 03:06:57,000
Boat, boat, boat is over here.

2887
03:06:58,940 --> 03:07:01,760
See, if I use a weapon on it, it actually gets destroyed.

2888
03:07:02,920 --> 03:07:06,740
Is this the first time that I have ever actually collected grass?

2889
03:07:08,040 --> 03:07:09,900
I thought you just couldn't do that.

2890
03:07:11,400 --> 03:07:15,700
But with the shear, everything is possible.

2891
03:07:19,020 --> 03:07:22,640
Don't think I've ever collected grass before.

2892
03:07:29,860 --> 03:07:31,700
So much delightful grass.

2893
03:07:32,300 --> 03:07:33,080
I have enough, though.

2894
03:07:33,160 --> 03:07:33,780
Look at all this grass.

2895
03:07:34,280 --> 03:07:35,420
That should be more than enough.

2896
03:07:40,620 --> 03:07:40,920
Bamboo?

2897
03:07:42,700 --> 03:07:44,220
I guess it would be nice to have some of that.

2898
03:07:54,170 --> 03:07:54,650
That's it!

2899
03:07:56,730 --> 03:07:57,050
Vines!

2900
03:07:58,370 --> 03:08:00,030
Now the question is how do I collect it?

2901
03:08:00,110 --> 03:08:01,070
It's got to be with the shears.

2902
03:08:04,230 --> 03:08:08,410
Just snip, snip, you know, snip them off, bring them home.

2903
03:08:18,570 --> 03:08:19,010
Yep.

2904
03:08:19,010 --> 03:08:19,670
That's right.

2905
03:08:20,270 --> 03:08:25,710
I was like, I remembered seeing those things on sides of buildings, but it was actually trees that I saw them on the side of.

2906
03:08:27,170 --> 03:08:27,930
Of course.

2907
03:08:28,990 --> 03:08:34,650
But they're a little... They're a little too jungly for me.

2908
03:08:34,870 --> 03:08:37,070
I feel like I've seen other versions of this.

2909
03:08:38,090 --> 03:08:39,550
That grew on walls.

2910
03:08:39,670 --> 03:08:43,630
Not growing out of the walls, but they grew along the walls of a building or something.

2911
03:08:46,100 --> 03:08:47,020
You know?

2912
03:08:51,660 --> 03:08:52,780
Let's try it.

2913
03:08:58,500 --> 03:08:59,260
Oh!

2914
03:08:59,780 --> 03:09:00,060
Oh!

2915
03:09:03,440 --> 03:09:05,080
Wait a minute.

2916
03:09:05,220 --> 03:09:07,060
I just unlocked a bunch of new things!

2917
03:09:07,980 --> 03:09:09,240
What the hell?

2918
03:09:11,060 --> 03:09:12,360
That is glorious.

2919
03:09:15,380 --> 03:09:16,500
Oh, yeah!

2920
03:09:20,380 --> 03:09:22,260
Oh, yeah, dude.

2921
03:09:23,260 --> 03:09:24,480
Oh, watch this!

2922
03:09:24,940 --> 03:09:25,920
It's so smart.

2923
03:09:30,820 --> 03:09:34,760
Uh... Uh, scaffolding?

2924
03:09:35,800 --> 03:09:36,800
Damn it.

2925
03:09:40,720 --> 03:09:41,380
Ah, whatever.

2926
03:09:41,680 --> 03:09:42,180
It's fine.

2927
03:09:44,400 --> 03:09:46,160
I'll just take from the bottom.

2928
03:09:48,540 --> 03:09:51,080
Oh wait, I can actually just use my thingy.

2929
03:10:08,970 --> 03:10:09,290
Nice.

2930
03:10:22,810 --> 03:10:25,370
I wonder how this is gonna look... on my building.

2931
03:10:32,350 --> 03:10:35,670
I think with the trapdoors that I have planned, it's gonna look super sweet.

2932
03:10:46,400 --> 03:10:46,860
Oh, wait.

2933
03:10:47,960 --> 03:10:48,240
Oh!

2934
03:10:48,640 --> 03:10:50,900
That removes the... Oh, but that breaks it.

2935
03:10:53,120 --> 03:10:54,420
Ooh, okay, yeah, you can't do that.

2936
03:10:58,470 --> 03:10:58,870
Nice.

2937
03:10:59,330 --> 03:11:01,150
Ah, here's the thing we're gonna do.

2938
03:11:02,510 --> 03:11:05,050
I kind of ran out, so I'm gonna go along this side.

2939
03:11:05,510 --> 03:11:06,690
And just keep doing it here.

2940
03:11:07,470 --> 03:11:09,490
Oh wait, can I not just... Oh!

2941
03:11:11,210 --> 03:11:12,830
Oh, but actually, it is worse.

2942
03:11:13,330 --> 03:11:14,450
I don't want to do that anyway.

2943
03:11:16,430 --> 03:11:17,270
This is faster.

2944
03:11:18,930 --> 03:11:19,650
Much faster.

2945
03:11:21,310 --> 03:11:22,710
Down, down, down, down.

2946
03:11:22,910 --> 03:11:24,790
And then from here, we're gonna go like that.

2947
03:11:26,540 --> 03:11:27,580
Get rid of that.

2948
03:11:29,260 --> 03:11:30,100
Can I walk on that?

2949
03:11:30,280 --> 03:11:30,480
Yeah.

2950
03:11:36,380 --> 03:11:37,480
Not bad at all.

2951
03:11:47,660 --> 03:11:50,600
Honestly, probably just easier to go from tree to tree and take the bottom.

2952
03:11:51,020 --> 03:11:52,340
Oh god, that broke.

2953
03:11:55,390 --> 03:11:56,190
That was fast.

2954
03:11:58,450 --> 03:11:59,250
Well, I have enough.

2955
03:12:00,670 --> 03:12:01,610
I like what I have.

2956
03:12:01,950 --> 03:12:03,250
So this looks a little different.

2957
03:12:03,370 --> 03:12:03,710
What is that?

2958
03:12:03,930 --> 03:12:05,130
Oh, I can't take it now!

2959
03:12:06,010 --> 03:12:07,130
Oh, no.

2960
03:12:08,970 --> 03:12:09,370
What?

2961
03:12:11,610 --> 03:12:12,010
Shit.

2962
03:12:12,210 --> 03:12:12,670
What is this?

2963
03:12:14,510 --> 03:12:15,090
Oh, well.

2964
03:12:16,050 --> 03:12:17,670
I mean, I got a lot of stuff.

2965
03:12:20,190 --> 03:12:20,910
Jungle leaves.

2966
03:12:26,260 --> 03:12:26,920
I'm okay.

2967
03:12:27,340 --> 03:12:27,900
Back home.

2968
03:12:38,800 --> 03:12:40,620
When am I able to see the ugly tower?

2969
03:12:41,660 --> 03:12:42,360
Let's see.

2970
03:12:46,500 --> 03:12:48,580
This will actually be a test of distance.

2971
03:12:58,710 --> 03:13:03,330
Should be... right here.

2972
03:13:10,670 --> 03:13:12,030
Oh, fuck!

2973
03:13:15,530 --> 03:13:18,990
It ran cold down my back.

2974
03:13:22,210 --> 03:13:23,870
